{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/981855-geeky-parenting","id":981855,"title":"Geeky Parenting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-04T18:05:20-07:00","id":981855,"title":"Geeky Parenting?","content":"I was wondering if there were any other parents here?<br /> <br /> I have one daughter and one on the way and while my current daughter is a bit young, I am anxious to introduce her to all of my geeky hobbies including RPG's. Has anybody else here introduced their kids to role playing? If so, at what age and when? If not that, then other geeky activities or entertainment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:43:06-07:00","id":981890,"title":"","content":"No kids of my own, but I was a nanny for a little while, and I introduced the kids to gaming. The first family I nannied for, the kids were too young (two and five), but the second family's kids were five and eight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:52:03-07:00","id":981894,"title":"","content":"Cool, what game was it and how did they like it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:18:38-07:00","id":981927,"title":"","content":"I have a one year old and another due in in march lord help me.<br /> <br /> My daughters still to young but she sits in on game night, i read rpg books to her and tell her she can play with us when shes a bit older. I think 4 or 5 is a good age to reallly get them into it. Old enough to start learning basic rules and can focus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:02:00-07:00","id":981941,"title":"","content":"Mine's going to be five in a few months. Think gaming will have to wait a couple years but we'll try something like Dungeons and Dragons first. Probably not start with the actual game so much as the co-operative storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:40:38-07:00","id":981956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/981855-geeky-parenting?p=981941#post981941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine's going to be five in a few months. Think gaming will have to wait a couple years but we'll try something like Dungeons and Dragons first. Probably not start with the actual game so much as the co-operative storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah thats what i was thinking, more free form, and introducing the rules bit by bit so as to not overwhelm their little brains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:32:35-07:00","id":982011,"title":"","content":"There is a kinda fantastic game for young kids, though fun for all ages available from drive thru rpg. Fairy tale deluxe it's a very simple system and you play little faries helping cute animals and kids in a magical forest. It was created by the author to get his little girls into gaming and his normal group plays it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:40:11-07:00","id":982079,"title":"","content":"There are a bunch of RPG games for kids. I've head good things about Happy Birthday Robot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:19:39-07:00","id":982185,"title":"","content":"DriveThruRPG has a kids bundle on their site for $20, Fairy Tale Deluxe and others are included, one hell of a deal.<br /> <br /> My 2 Baby Bears don't really need a lot of help coming up with pretend things to play, and rules would just get in their way at this stage (6 and 4). A couple of years from now, they might be ready for it. I'll try out a few now.<br /> <br /> As far as other &quot;geeky&quot; things, they like Star Wars but more in theory than practice: they have yet to sit thru the original in full, but the oldest Baby Bear will watch the Lego Star Wars and Rebels. They like superheroes, they've watched Justice League and Avengers: Earth's Mightiest Heroes almost from beginning to end. They've watched several of the Marvel Cinematic movies with us (no Deadpool, they're too young, but that shit was funny!) and almost stand still/stay awake for Agents of SHIELD (not this season, though, it's on too late at night). They want to play Wii and Playstation with me, the former they're getting the hang of, the latter they're still struggling with the controls.<br /> <br /> They're also still little girls, so they still get excited over dolls, ponies and pretty/cute things, so before anyone goes down that path, they're just going to be well rounded. They might play superheroes with the boys, but they want to be Wonder Woman, Batgirl, Black Widow, or Supergirl. they are my Warrior Princesses, they will kick ass and takes names and look <i><b>FABULOUS </b></i>doing it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 10-05-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:27:53-07:00","id":982657,"title":"","content":"I've got a 14 year old son. He's been gaming with me for a while now. He even tried his hand at storytelling for a few sessions, but felt overwhelmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They call me... Mr. Demmywinks.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1210-demetrius7997","name":"Demetrius7997","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:01:19-07:00","id":982698,"title":"","content":"My suggestion for RPG for +6 children is &quot;Magissa&quot; but I don't know about any English languange version yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:51:48-07:00","id":988839,"title":"","content":"If you are looking for a rules light game to introduce new players, then Risus is the best way to go. Rules are simple, combat is fast, general theme can be silly (or serious, depending on what you want out of a game) and the game's free as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/981855-geeky-parenting#post981855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one daughter and one on the way and while my current daughter is a bit young, I am anxious to introduce her to all of my geeky hobbies including RPG's. Has anybody else here introduced their kids to role playing? If so, at what age and when? If not that, then other geeky activities or entertainment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bedtime stories. Read books to her, spark her imagination, introduce her to the world of fantasy. With a bit of luck she'll start to read on her own later both to learn more stories and hopefully learn something. Then when she reaches a good age introduce her to roleplaying and you're done.<br /> <br /> But, and this is the most important part: Accept it if she says no. Don't force your hobbies onto someone who's not interested, and pick up on it if they're just playing to please you. Playing with someone who doesn't want to is its very own circle of hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}